      "summary": "AOPC favors IG; Lung Focus Score favors Grad-CAM.",
      "explanation": "AOPC measures whether removing highlighted pixels reduces model confidence (faithfulness), while LFS measures whether mass falls inside an automatic lung mask (anatomical plausibility). Integrated Gradients often spread attribution across lung fields (higher AOPC potential but diffuse maps), whereas Grad-CAM peaks on discriminative conv features (sharper heatmaps, sometimes higher LFS when peaks align with lungs)."
